From 96c2d1357d89f7999e678cc7be5c646a3032f40d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 14:01:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] armchina-npu: drop redundant pm_runtime_enable in ACPI
 probe loop

The ACPI bus enables runtime PM for child devices via acpi_bind_one().
sky1_npu_probe ACPI branch then calls pm_runtime_enable() again per
NPU core, which trips the kernel's 'Unbalanced pm_runtime_enable!'
warning (once per core, 3 lines in dmesg) because disable_depth is
already 0.

The warning is non-fatal; probe continues and /dev/aipu binds cleanly.
But it pollutes the dmesg first-boot record + diagnostics dumps. Drop
the line + add a comment explaining why.

Validated on cixmini .66 (kernel 7.0.9-cix-sky1-next): probe still
binds to ACPI CIXH4000:00, all 3 cores attach via dev_pm_domain_attach,
no Unbalanced pm_runtime_enable warnings.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 driver/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/driver/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c b/driver/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
index 99c9650..f592445 100644
--- a/driver/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
+++ b/driver/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
@@ -392,9 +392,17 @@ static int sky1_npu_probe(struct platform_device *p_dev)
 		if (i == CIX_NPU_PD_NUM)
 			break;
                 acpi_bind_one(&(to_acpi_device_node(child)->dev), to_acpi_device_node(child));
-				cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i] = &(to_acpi_device_node(child)->dev);
-                pm_runtime_enable(cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i]);
-				dev_pm_domain_attach(&(to_acpi_device_node(child)->dev), true);
+                cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i] = &(to_acpi_device_node(child)->dev);
+                /*
+                 * Do NOT call pm_runtime_enable() here — the ACPI bus
+                 * already enables runtime PM for child devices when they
+                 * are probed via acpi_bind_one(). Calling it again
+                 * decrements disable_depth below 0 and trips the kernel's
+                 * "Unbalanced pm_runtime_enable!" warning at probe time,
+                 * once per core, polluting dmesg even though the driver
+                 * otherwise functions.
+                 */
+                dev_pm_domain_attach(&(to_acpi_device_node(child)->dev), true);
                 i++;
             }
         }
